{#- Rendered into user prompts. `ctx` is an app.ai.context.CandidateContext (all optional). -#}
{% set stages = {
  "student": "student or recent graduate, little or no full-time work history yet",
  "entry": "entry level, in the first year or two of work",
  "mid": "mid-level, several years of experience",
  "senior": "senior, many years of experience and often leading others",
  "career_changer": "career changer, moving into this field from a different one",
} %}
{% if ctx is defined and ctx %}
Target role: {{ ctx.target_role or "not specified" }}
Field: {{ ctx.industry or "not specified" }}
{% if ctx.experience_level %}
Career stage: {{ stages[ctx.experience_level] }}
{% endif %}
{% if ctx.spelling == "en_gb" %}
Spelling: British English (organise, colour, programme, licence). Use it in everything you write.
{% elif ctx.spelling == "en_us" %}
Spelling: American English (organize, color, program, license). Use it in everything you write.
{% endif %}
{% if ctx.impact_language %}
Results that matter in this field: {{ ctx.impact_language }}
{% endif %}
{% if ctx.fresher %}

Fresher mode: this candidate has little or no full-time experience. Build on what they do have: their education (course, modules, grades, dissertation or final project), projects, internships and placements, part-time jobs, volunteering and extracurricular roles. Show the transferable skills these prove (for example teamwork from a group project, customer care from a weekend job, organisation from running a society). A short work history is normal here and is not a weakness.
{% elif ctx.career_changer %}

Career changer mode: this candidate is moving into {{ ctx.industry or "this field" }} from a different one. Find the transferable skills in their earlier career that the target role needs, and describe that earlier work in words the new field recognises (for example a retail manager's rota planning and team leadership for an operations role, or a nurse's patient education for a teaching role). Never claim experience in the new field that they don't have, and don't dismiss the earlier career as irrelevant.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
